# Managed by Ansible (eve_autoclean role). Do not edit by hand.
#
# Lets the low-disk LaunchAgent run eve's privileged categories (system caches
# and logs, unified logs, sleepimage, hidden data directories, installer
# leftovers, snapshot thinning) without a GUI admin dialog, which under launchd
# would hang forever with nowhere to draw.
#
# WHY THIS IS NOW A REAL BOUNDARY
#
#   The grant names {{ eve_autoclean_helper }} — a root-owned, non-user-writable
#   copy installed by this role. The previous rule pointed at a script in the
#   operator's home directory and its own comment admitted the scoping was
#   "organisational, not a security boundary", because anything able to write
#   that file gained passwordless root.
#
#   The objection recorded then — not wanting to maintain a second copy of the
#   commands — no longer applies: the worker is the same binary in a different
#   mode, so there is nothing duplicated to drift.
#
#   eve verifies the ownership itself before using this path, and falls back to
#   re-executing the invoking binary if it is not root-owned and not group- or
#   world-writable. The role asserts the same thing after installing.
#
# WHAT ROOT ACTUALLY RECEIVES
#
#   A typed, validated plan on stdin — never a shell string. The worker re-runs
#   the entire safety funnel as root and does not trust the caller's verdict,
#   only its request. A compromised parent cannot talk it into deleting
#   something the protection policy forbids.
#
# The command path must match what eve executes, character for character;
# sudo does no interpreter or symlink resolution.
{{ eve_autoclean_user }} ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: {{ eve_autoclean_helper }} __worker
